# Vendored dependencies are somebody else's code, checked in so the build needs
# no network. Reviewing them is not the point of a pull request, and an update
# that touches hundreds of files buries the one file the change is about.
#
# linguist-vendored keeps them out of the language statistics and collapses
# them in a pull request. -diff is the same idea locally: git says the file
# differs rather than printing it. Pass --text to see it anyway.
vendor/** linguist-vendored
vendor/** -diff
